+  # Outcome report: tells the contributor *why* a check is red, so an
+  # infrastructure hang never masquerades as "your code failed".
+  # Three signals separate the two:
+  #   * needs.<job>.result == cancelled      -> the job itself hit its
+  #     timeout-minutes (runner never finished it; your code is innocent).
+  #   * failure_kind == step_timeout_or_infra -> a checkout/setup/install step
+  #     hit its step timeout (the classify steps export this); GitHub reports
+  #     such a job as "failure", which is exactly what used to be misread as
+  #     a contributor failure.
+  #   * failed with no classification output at all -> the job died before any
+  #     step ran (action-download / runner-allocation outage, e.g. the
+  #     2026-08-06 incident on bottube#1639/#1640). Also infrastructure.
+  # Only a plain step exit-code failure is blamed on the contributor.
   report:
     name: CI outcome report
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
